{
  "_comment": "Printed section headings mapped to the five canonical names; 'other' is split into labels that become original_name. Headings are compared after normalising: lower case, numbering, a trailing colon and a trailing count such as (5) removed, spaces collapsed. Experience rule: only headings that list positions held (Work Experience, Employment, Academic Positions, Teaching Experience, Research Experience) map to experience; headings that list courses taught, plain 'Teaching', responsibilities or projects (also 'Project Experience') map to other. Publications rule: papers presented, presentations, talks, posters and attended events map to other (presentations); book chapters stay in publications. Job titles and school-level labels (12th, HSC) are entry content, never headings. A heading not listed here is matched by fuzz.ratio (stage4_normalize.fuzzy_min), then by its content, then kept as other with a warning.",
  "_comment_exact_only": "exact_only: common academic CV headings added from general knowledge. They are matched only exactly (after the same normalising), never by fuzzy match, and an alias listed above always wins. Hyphen and '&' variants are listed separately because normalising does not change them.",
